  "term": "attack behavior",
  "definition": "Attack behavior is aggressive action directed at another individual, used in this source as a measure of increased aggression after traumatic or stressful experience. In the study context, it refers to recurrent or excessive attacking that can persist over time and is linked to activation of brain circuits involving the medial amygdala.",
